Subject: Poll interrupts on the back edge

What this does
  Poll interrupts on the back edge.

Why we need it
  A loop with no calls never reached `JS_SetInterruptHandler`: the back edge only checked the DRC parked set, so `while (true) {}` and `for (;;) { i++; }` were uninterruptible.

What it adds
  The back edge decrements `ctx->interrupt_counter` and tail-calls a poll handler (which runs the DRC safepoint) at zero; a self-branch counts as a backward edge.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
